      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is often caused by broken vertex normals in worlds with bloom enabled. There doesn't seem to be a way to prevent it outright across all avatars and worlds, but the avatar's creator can fix this on the avatar by recalculating normals in Blender, or in Unity's mesh import settings.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-03-21T00:24:05.727Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It seems some avatars have very strange effect when shaders are blocked.\nNormally if everything is blocked except normal avatar itself, it should not have special lights.\n\nUnfortunately, some avatars have unexpected strong \"flashlight\" effect. It can hurt some eyes and i see it sometimes in the some worlds. Also bad for people with epilepsy!\n\nExample: https://clips.twitch.tv/HilariousTawdryStrawberryEagleEye\n\nThis flashlight MUST blocked if i have all effects blocked (no shaders and extra animations) but why is this not blocked?\n\nPlease do something about it, it's VERY annoying effect.",
